# council

Convenes the full Three-Agent Council (`claude`, `codex`, `agy`) through the shared `peer-consult` orchestrator.
All three agents independently analyze your packet in genuinely read-only environments, critique anonymized proposals (`Proposal A`, `Proposal B`, `Proposal C`), and produce a Chair Synthesis with explicit unresolved disagreements, evidence ledger, and assumptions ledger.

## Recursion rule
If `PEER_CONSULT_DEPTH` is set (you are yourself an adviser or council member), never invoke `peer-consult`. The orchestrator refuses mechanically outside model prompts.

## 1. Build the packet
Write a UTF-8 JSON packet to a fresh path in {{TEMP_WHERE}} (never inside the repository):

```json
{
  "task_id": "short-stable-id-for-this-task",
  "question": "The exact architecture, debugging, or implementation question",
  "help_type": "diagnosis | design_critique | experiment_review | code_review | other",
  "help_type_detail": "required when help_type is other",
  "goal": "What the overall task is trying to achieve",
  "constraints": ["hard requirements, versions, budgets"],
  "tried": ["what you already tried and what happened"],
  "observations": ["actual errors, measurements, logs"],
  "hypothesis": "your current hypothesis (labelled unverified)",
  "snippets": [{"label": "context", "path": "src/x.py", "lines": "10-50", "content": "..."}],
  "files": [{"path": "src/y.py", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 100}]
}
```

