## 3. Workflow & Gates
- **`council discuss`**: Runs Stage 1 (3 concurrent read-only proposals) -> Stage 2 (anonymized cross-critique) -> Stage 3 (Chair synthesis) and completes with JSON + Markdown report (`report_markdown_path`).
- **`council plan`**: Runs Stages 1–3, synthesizes `authorized_files`, `acceptance_criteria`, and `recommended_writer`, and pauses in `AWAITING_APPROVAL` with an `approval_token`.
- **`council execute`**: Requires explicit `--approve` (or `--approval-token`). **Only the human user can approve.** Show the user the synthesized plan (`authorized_files`, `acceptance_criteria`, risks) and run `execute --approve` only after they explicitly approve that plan in this conversation; never approve your own plan. Creates an isolated Git worktree (`council/<run_id>`), locks a single writer, verifies file scope before/after writes, runs deterministic tests, collects read-only peer reviews from the other two agents, and allows at most 2 controlled repair attempts. Never auto-merges or deploys.
- **`council status` / `resume` / `cancel` / `report` / `doctor` / `office`**: Inspect runs, resume from SQLite checkpoints without repeating completed stages, cancel active process trees, render Markdown/JSON reports, or open the real-time Pixel-Art AI Council Office UI.
